A reference / link / binary chunk, focused (one walkable stop)
description: the chapter_atom_focused state
- >
  A RAW pointer chunk hosts the source editor's own reference cells (a nested editor over a
  one-entry wrapper - the pick machinery, verbatim); links and binaries are read-only stops. THE
  BOUNDARY HAND-OFF - the wrapper holds exactly ONE atom, so on the IDLE atom every walking key
  leaves the chunk through the CHAPTER machine instead of ringing at the sub-editor's edge; while
  PICKING the kit owns every key (dropdown arrows, the cell walk)
- !!<*yamlover: $defs: table>
  header:
    - Event
      width: 2
    - 'Condition / note'
      width: 4
    - 'Next state'
      width: 2
  - ['`enter`', 'a pointer atom - the reference opens for retargeting (the source grammar''s pick)', '[pointer_pick_editing](*::server:yamlover-editor:pointer_pick_editing)']
  - ['`enter`', 'a link / binary - nothing to edit - swallowed', '`chapter_atom_focused` (stays)']
  - ['`backspace`', 'a pointer atom - the emptied reference DISSOLVES the chunk into an empty paragraph, caret in it', '[chapter_prose_editing](*::server:chapter-editor:chapter_prose_editing)']
  - ['`backspace`', 'a link / binary - the chapter grammar leaves it standing', '`chapter_atom_focused` (stays)']
  - ['`up_down_arrow`', 'the walk continues past the atom (whatever cell is adjacent)', '[chapter_prose_editing](*::server:chapter-editor:chapter_prose_editing)']
  - ['`left_right_arrow`', 'an atom is ONE stop - any arrow leaves it', '[chapter_prose_editing](*::server:chapter-editor:chapter_prose_editing)']
  - ['`tab`', 'swallowed, never a browser focus walk', '[nop](*::server:yamlover-editor:nop)']
  - ['`alphanumeric`', 'typing into an atom does nothing here', '`chapter_atom_focused` (stays)']
